rations for every integer  \n\n\\[\nk=0,1,2,\\dots ,n .\n\\]\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### 5.  Final answer\n\nNo configuration can have more than \\(n\\) sunny lines because there are only \\(n\\) lines in total.  \nThe constructions above show that every integer between \\(0\\) and \\(n\\) inclusive is attainable.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\;k\\in\\{0,1,2,\\dots ,n\\}\\;}\n\\]"
