## 4.  Conclusion\n\nWe have exhibited:\n\n* a configuration with \\(k=0\\) sunny lines;\n* an impossibility proof showing that \\(k\\ge n-1\\) cannot occur;\n* a concrete construction that works for every integer \\(k\\) with \\(0\\le k\\le n-2\\).\n\nTherefore the set of admissible values of \\(k\\) is exactly  \n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\{0,1,2,\\dots ,n-2\\}} .\n\\]"
