\\{0,1,2,\\dots ,n+1\\}.\n\\]\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### 4.  Upper bound on the number of sunny lines\n\nA configuration consists of exactly \\(n\\) lines, so it cannot contain more than \\(n\\) sunny lines. Hence any admissible \\(k\\) must satisfy \\(k\\le n\\).\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### 5.  Conclusion\n\nThe base case and the inductive step show that for each \\(n\\ge 3\\) every integer \\(k\\) with \\(0\\le k\\le n\\) can be realized, and the trivial upper bound shows that no larger \\(k\\) is possible. Therefore the set of all admissible values of \\(k\\) is  \n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\{0,1,2,\\dots ,n\\}} .\n\\]"
