can have fewer than \\(\\lceil n/2\\rceil\\) sunny lines.  \n- The construction above shows that for every integer \\(k\\) with \\(\\lceil n/2\\rceil\\le k\\le n\\) there exists a configuration of \\(n\\) distinct lines satisfying the covering condition and containing exactly \\(k\\) sunny lines.\n\nHence the set of admissible values of \\(k\\) is precisely  \n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\; \\left\\lceil \\dfrac{n}{2}\\right\\rceil,\\; \\left\\lceil \\dfrac{n}{2}\\right\\rceil+1,\\dots ,\\, n\\; } .\n\\]"
