e intercept \\(\\beta_j\\) is chosen so that \\(M_j\\) passes through the point\n   \\((v+j,\\,1)\\) of the \\((v+j)\\)-th column:\n\n   \\[\n   \\beta_j = 1-\\alpha_j (v+j).\n   \\]\n\n   Because \\(\\alpha_j\\neq0,-1\\), each line \\(M_j\\) is sunny.\n\n   *Verification.*  \n\n   - **Columns \\(1,\\dots ,v\\).**  \n     Every point of these columns lies on the corresponding vertical line \\(L_i\\).\n\n   - **Column \\(v+j\\) (\\(1\\le j\\le k\\)).**  \n     The points of \\(S_n\\) in this column are\n     \\[\n     (v+j,1),\\;(v+j,2),\\dots ,\\bigl(v+j,\\;n+1-(v+j)\\bigr).\n     \\]\n     The line \\(M_j\\) supplies the point \\((v+j,1)\\) by construction.\n     For each \\(t\\ge2\\) the point \\((v+j,t)\\) lies on the vertical line\n     \\(L_t\\) (because \\(t\\le v\\) – recall that \\(v\\ge2\\) and \\(t\\le n+1-(v+j)\\le v\\)).\n     Hence every point of the column is covered.\n\n   - **Distinctness.**  \n     The vertical lines are pairwise distinct.  \n     The sunny lines have distinct slopes \\(\\alpha_j\\), so they are distinct from each other\n     and from the vertical lines.\n\n   Consequently the \\(n\\) lines \\(\\{L_i\\}_{i=1}^{v}\\cup\\{M_j\\}_{j=1}^{k}\\) cover all points of\n   \\(S_n\\) and contain exactly \\(k\\) sunny lines.\n\n6. **Conclusion.**  \n   Lemma 2 forces \\(v\\ge2\\), i.e. \\(k\\le n-2\\).  \n   The construction above shows that every integer \\(k\\) with \\(0\\le k\\le n-2\\) is attainable.  \n   Therefore the set of all admissible values of \\(k\\) is precisely  \n\n   \\[\n   \\boxed{\\{\\,k\\in\\mathbb Z_{\\ge0}\\mid 0\\le k\\le n-2\\,\\}} .\n   \\]\n\n\n### Verification Task Reminder ###\n\nYour task is to act as an IMO grader. Now, generate the **summary** and the **step-by-step verification log** for the solution above. In your log, justify each correct step and explain in detail any errors or justification gaps you find, as specified in the instructions above.\n\n"
