ion  \n\nFor every integer \\(n\\ge 3\\) we have exhibited an explicit configuration of \\(n\\) distinct lines that\n\n* covers all points \\((a,b)\\) with \\(a,b\\ge 1\\) and \\(a+b\\le n+1\\);\n* contains exactly one sunny line.\n\nHence the integer  \n\n\\[\n\\boxed{k=1}\n\\]\n\nis always attainable. The existence of configurations with other values of \\(k\\) remains open."
